      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1025794352,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@rbalint I want to give you a heads-up. We would actually prefer moving directly to 5.12, but there are some Linux derivates out there which we still support, that would be affected by that. The discussion at SF22US has had the following concession:\n\n* Recommendation for building Wireshark 4.0 will be Qt 6.x (probably 6.3.1)\n* Support for building Wireshark 4.0 with Qt 5 will require at least 5.12\n* Support for building Wireshark 4.0 with Qt 5 version 5.10 and 5.11 will be possible, but present a warning during configuration\n* Wireshark 3.6 will continue to support Qt 5.9 and higher",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
